  "conops_note": "\u00a73.1's share-isolation rule is written as a rule about how shares are created. This finding is about a share nobody created on purpose: a probe's artifact, kept so a later probe could reuse it, carrying the base table for as long as it sat there. The control that catches it is not a naming convention, it is a periodic metastore-wide assertion that no base table appears in any share -- which is what scripts/24 rule 1 is, and what v1.6 should require as a standing check rather than a publish-time one."
